@@ -0,0 +1,113 @@
+# Live Hermes Modification: First-Class Domain Modules
+
+Date: 2026-06-15
+Status: applied to Emo's live Hermes runtime branch
+
+## Intent
+
+Reintroduce Domain Modules as a first-class Hermes primitive between always-on memory and procedural skills.
+
+Domain Modules are dense, task-scoped background context. They are explicitly **not** skills and must not be injected with “follow its instructions” semantics.
+
+## Runtime storage
+
+Domain Modules live under the active Hermes home:
+
+```text
+$HERMES_HOME/domain-modules/<name>/MODULE.md
+$HERMES_HOME/domain-modules/<name>/references/*
+$HERMES_HOME/domain-modules/<name>/templates/*
+$HERMES_HOME/domain-modules/<name>/assets/*
+```
+
+`MODULE.md` must have YAML frontmatter with:
+
+```yaml
+---
+kind: domain-module
+name: <module-name>
+description: <short description>
+---
+```
+
+## Tool surface
+
+Adds the `domain_modules` toolset and includes these tools in core tool discovery:
+
+- `domain_modules_list`
+- `domain_module_view`
+- `domain_module_manage`
+
+Implementation file:
+
+- `tools/domain_modules_tool.py`
+
+## Cron support
+
+Cron jobs can carry:
+
+```yaml
+domain_modules:
+  - local-inference-domain-module
+```
+
+At prompt-build time, cron injects Domain Modules as:
+
+```text
+[DOMAIN MODULE: "..." — task-scoped background context, not procedural instructions.]
+...
+[/DOMAIN MODULE: "..."]
+```
+
+This remains distinct from skill injection, which intentionally says the user invoked a skill and wants its instructions followed.
+
+Changed files:
+
+- `cron/jobs.py`
+- `cron/scheduler.py`
+- `tools/cronjob_tools.py`
+- `toolsets.py`
+
+## Validation receipt
+
+From worktree `/Users/emo/.hermes/hermes-agent.worktrees/domain-modules-runtime-20260615`:
+
+```bash
+python -m py_compile tools/domain_modules_tool.py tools/cronjob_tools.py cron/jobs.py cron/scheduler.py toolsets.py
+uv run ruff check tools/domain_modules_tool.py tools/cronjob_tools.py cron/jobs.py cron/scheduler.py toolsets.py tests/tools/test_domain_modules_tool.py tests/cron/test_domain_modules_cron.py
+uv run pytest tests/tools/test_domain_modules_tool.py tests/cron/test_domain_modules_cron.py tests/cron/test_scheduler.py::TestBuildJobPromptMissingSkill tests/cron/test_scheduler.py::TestBuildJobPromptBumpUse -q -o 'addopts='
+```
+
+Result: `16 passed`.
+
+Live smoke checked:
+
+- module create/list succeeds against a temp `domain-modules` root
+- `local-inference-domain-module` loads
+- generated module context contains `task-scoped background context`
+- generated module context does **not** contain `follow its instructions`
+- model tool discovery for `domain_modules` exposes all three new tools
+- cron prompt injection includes background context and excludes skill-instruction language when only modules are attached
+
+## Reapply checklist after upstream update
+
+If a future `hermes update` drops local runtime modifications:
+
+1. Check whether upstream now has equivalent Domain Module support:
+   ```bash
+   git grep -n "domain_modules_list\|domain_module_view\|domain_module_manage\|kind: domain-module"
+   ```
+2. If absent, reapply this patch intent by restoring/porting:
+   - `tools/domain_modules_tool.py`
+   - `toolsets.py` core/toolset registration
+   - cron storage field `domain_modules` in `cron/jobs.py`
+   - cron prompt injection in `cron/scheduler.py`
+   - cron tool schema/API plumbing in `tools/cronjob_tools.py`
+   - tests in `tests/tools/test_domain_modules_tool.py` and `tests/cron/test_domain_modules_cron.py`
+3. Re-run the validation receipt above.
+4. Restart the gateway or start a fresh session so model tool schemas include the new Domain Module tools.
+
+## Caveats
+
+- Already-running Discord/gateway sessions will not see the new tool schemas until restart/fresh session.
+- Domain Modules are intentionally not loaded through `skill_view` and do not count as procedural skill invocations.
